## Change 3 — `src/app/man/admin/report/[reportId]/page.tsx`

**What:** Make the review page work during `generating` status — poll for updates and render whatever sections exist, with skeleton placeholders for sections not yet generated.

### 3a — Allow access during generation

Currently the page shows `"Report not found or still generating."` if `report_data` is null. Remove this gate. The page should render even with partial data.

Also:
- The auto-transition `draft_ready → in_review` on page open should be skipped if status is `generating`

### 3b — Poll while generating

Add a `useEffect` that polls `GET /api/man-report/:reportId` every **3 seconds** while `report.status === 'generating'`. Stop polling when status changes to anything else.

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (report?.status !== 'generating') return;
  const interval = setInterval(load, 3000);
  return () => clearInterval(interval);
}, [report?.status]);
```

### 3c — Live generation indicator

When status is `generating`, show a "Live" indicator in the review panel header:

```
● LIVE · Generating S3 – Chromatic Harmony…
```

Map the `progress_stage` value to a human-readable label:

```typescript
const STAGE_LABELS: Record<string, string> = {
  classifying:       'Classifying profile…',
  generating_s1:     'Writing Face Architecture…',
  generating_s2:     'Writing Body Geometry…',
  generating_s3:     'Writing Chromatic Harmony…',
  generating_s4:     'Writing 16 Outfits…',
  generating_s5:     'Writing Style Rules…',
  generating_s6:     'Writing Identity Statement…',
  generating_images: 'Generating images…',
  finalising:        'Finalising…',
};
```

### 3d — Section skeletons for incomplete sections

In the section list in the right panel, each section row should show:

- `●` green dot + section text if that section is complete in `report_data.sections`
- `○` grey pulsing shimmer if section is not yet generated

The `<ManReport>` component on the left should not break on missing sections. Pass empty string or `null` for sections not yet populated — `ManReport` should skip rendering a section if its content is empty.

> **Note:** `ManReport.tsx` likely already handles empty strings gracefully since sections are strings. Verify this — if it renders empty headers, add a guard: `if (!section) return null`.

### 3e — Admin can approve completed sections immediately

The approve toggle should work on any section that has content — even while generation is still running. This is the main QC benefit. No change needed to the approval logic itself; just make sure the UI doesn't block approval during `generating` status.

