## What Does NOT Change

- The classification prompt (Prompt 1) — untouched
- The section content/quality — same prompts, just called individually
- Image generation — identical to today
- `ManReport.tsx` component — only needs a guard for empty sections (minor)
- All other API routes — untouched
- The public client report page — untouched
- Database schema — no new columns. `report_data` JSONB already supports partial writes

---

## Risk: Does splitting into 6 calls change quality?

Minimal risk. Each section call receives the **full classification JSON** as context — the same structured data the single call used. The classification is comprehensive enough that section-level context is fully preserved. The only thing lost is cross-section "cohesion" that Gemini might have had when writing all 6 in one pass — but in practice the classification JSON already encodes that cohesion. Section 4 (outfits) already references the colour palette and body rules from the classification, not from section 3's prose.

